tengine/godot/pulls/109511","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109511","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109511.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109511.patch","merged_at":"2025-10-27T15:06:22Z"},"body":"If you open `Label25k.tscn` in the test project below, and then attempt to delete one of the elements by selecting it in the scene tree dock and then pressing delete, it takes ~12 seconds for me without this PR. With this PR, it's less than half a second.\r\n\r\nHere's the flamegraph showing the problem:\r\n<img width=\"2530\" height=\"1294\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7ab528fe-4585-4f0d-861b-cc8c38b28739\" />\r\n\r\nThe `SceneTreeEditor` change take the performance from terrible to usable, getting the time down to under a second by itself.\r\n\r\nThe `Tree` `Vector` -> `LocalVector` change only makes hundreds of ms worth of difference, but that's enough to bring it from usable to pretty good. It's the less important of the two, if it's objectionable.\r\n\r\n---------------------\r\n\r\nAll performance tests were run on builds made with the following command: `scons optimize=speed_trace debug_symbols=yes platform=linuxbsd dev_build=no production=yes`\r\n\r\nThe test project [editor-optimization-test-scenes.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21709465/editor-optimization-test-scenes.zip) consists of a series of scenes that each have 25,000 of a common type of node.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/use